### =====================================================================
### Endpoint tests - Sistema complet amb autenticació i CRUD
### Use with the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or adapt to Postman).
### Start the server first:  npm run dev   (default port 3001)
###
### Auth is cookie-based: POST /login sets an httpOnly "access_token"
### cookie (1h). REST Client stores that cookie and sends it on the
### following requests, so run the file top to bottom.
### Run the "no auth" section BEFORE the login section (or after /logout).
### =====================================================================

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3001
@username = apitest
@password = secret123


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 1. AUTH - no session yet
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 1.1 Protected page without login -> 403 "Access not authorized"
GET {{baseUrl}}/protected

### 1.2 Books CRUD without login -> 403 "Access not authorized"
GET {{baseUrl}}/books

### 1.3 Magazines CRUD without login -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/magazines

### 1.4 Books JSON without login -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/1

### 1.5 Create a book without login -> 403 (nothing written to db.json)
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Should not be created",
  "author": "Nobody",
  "year": 2000
}


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 2. AUTH - register / login / logout
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 2.1 Register a new user -> 200 { "id": "<uuid>" } + access_token cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2.2 Register with the same username -> 400 "username already exists"
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2.3 Register with a too-short username -> 400 "Username superior a 3 caracteres"
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "ab",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2.4 Register with a too-short password -> 400 "password superior a 5 caracteres"
POST {{baseUrl}}/register
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "apitest2",
  "password": "123"
}

### 2.5 Login with a wrong password -> 401 "password is invalid"
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "wrong-password"
}

### 2.6 Login with an unknown user -> 401 "username does not exist"
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "nobody_here",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2.7 Login OK -> 200 { user, token } + access_token cookie (1h)
POST {{baseUrl}}/login
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "username": "{{username}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}

### 2.8 Protected page with session -> 200 HTML (protected.ejs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/protected

### 2.9 Profile / index pages
GET {{baseUrl}}/


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 3. BOOKS CRUD  (/books) - needs the cookie from 2.7
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 3.1 GET all books -> HTML page (books.ejs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books

### 3.2 GET form to create a book -> HTML (new_book.ejs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/new

### 3.3 GET one book -> 200 JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/1

### 3.4 GET edit form for a book -> HTML (edit_books.ejs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/1/edit

### 3.5 CREATE a book (JSON) -> 302 redirect to /books
### The new id is max(existing ids) + 1, so it will be 5 on a fresh db.json.
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dune",
  "author": "Frank Herbert",
  "year": 1965
}

### 3.6 CREATE a book (HTML form style, urlencoded) -> 302 redirect to /books
POST {{baseUrl}}/books
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

name=Neuromancer&author=William+Gibson&year=1984

### 3.7 GET the book created in 3.5
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/5

### 3.8 UPDATE a book (real PUT, JSON) -> 200 { "message": "Book updated successfully" }
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books/5
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dune (Edició revisada)",
  "year": 1966
}

### 3.9 UPDATE a book via HTML form (POST + _method=PUT) -> 302 redirect to /books
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/5?_method=PUT
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

name=Dune&author=Frank+Herbert&year=1965

### 3.10 UPDATE a book that does not exist -> 404 "Book not found"
PUT {{baseUrl}}/books/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Ghost"
}

### 3.11 DELETE a book (real DELETE) -> 200 { "message": "Book deleted successfully" }
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/5

### 3.12 DELETE a book via HTML form (POST + _method=DELETE) -> 302 redirect to /books
POST {{baseUrl}}/books/4?_method=DELETE

### 3.13 DELETE a book that does not exist -> 404 "Book not found"
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/books/999

### 3.14 GET a book that does not exist
### NOTE: current code does res.json(undefined) here, so it answers 200 with an
### empty body instead of 404. Expected behaviour is 404 - worth fixing.
GET {{baseUrl}}/books/999


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 4. MAGAZINES CRUD  (/magazines) - needs the cookie from 2.7
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 4.1 GET all magazines -> HTML page (magazines.ejs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/magazines

### 4.2 GET form to create a magazine -> HTML (new_magazine.ejs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/magazines/new

### 4.3 GET one magazine -> 200 JSON
GET {{baseUrl}}/magazines/1

### 4.4 GET one magazine that does not exist -> 404 "Magazine not found"
GET {{baseUrl}}/magazines/999

### 4.5 GET edit form for a magazine -> HTML (edit_magazines.ejs)
GET {{baseUrl}}/magazines/1/edit

### 4.6 CREATE a magazine (JSON) -> 302 redirect to /magazines
### id will be 4 on a fresh db.json.
POST {{baseUrl}}/magazines
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Nature",
  "issue": 650,
  "publisher": "Springer Nature",
  "category": "Science & Nature",
  "publication_date": "2024-04-04"
}

### 4.7 GET the magazine created in 4.6
GET {{baseUrl}}/magazines/4

### 4.8 UPDATE a magazine (real PUT, JSON) -> 200 { "message": "Magazine updated successfully" }
PUT {{baseUrl}}/magazines/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "issue": 651
}

### 4.9 UPDATE a magazine via HTML form (POST + _method=PUT) -> 302 redirect to /magazines
POST {{baseUrl}}/magazines/4?_method=PUT
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

name=Nature&issue=652&publisher=Springer+Nature&category=Science+%26+Nature&publication_date=2024-04-04

### 4.10 UPDATE a magazine that does not exist -> 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/magazines/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "issue": 1
}

### 4.11 DELETE a magazine (real DELETE) -> 200 { "message": "Magazine deleted successfully" }
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/magazines/4

### 4.12 DELETE a magazine that does not exist -> 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/magazines/999


### ---------------------------------------------------------------------
### 5. LOGOUT
### ---------------------------------------------------------------------

### 5.1 Logout (JSON) -> clears access_token cookie
POST {{baseUrl}}/logout

### 5.2 After logout, a protected route is refused again -> 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/books

### 5.3 Logout via GET -> clears cookie and redirects to /
GET {{baseUrl}}/logout